.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-INSTALL-TARGET 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-install-target
.Nd install kldload from the live image onto a disk, from an answers file or by asking
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -config Ar answers.env
.Nm
.Fl -guided
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The installer the live image, the web console's install page and network
installs all end in.
It partitions the disk, makes the ZFS pool and its datasets \(em
encrypted when asked \(em installs the chosen distribution and profile
into the boot environment
.Pa rpool/ROOT/ Ns Ar hostname
from the image's offline mirrors, sets up ZFSBootMenu or the signed boot
path with Secure Boot, and writes the install manifest that
.Xr kldload-firstboot 8
reads.
It checks the result \(em a kernel on the target among other things
\(em rather than trusting each step's exit status.
.Pp
The host name is made lower case and checked: 1 to 63 letters, digits
and hyphens, starting with a letter.
If the install stops part-way the target is unmounted on the way out.
It runs itself with root's privileges.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -config Ar answers.env
Install unattended from an answers file.
.It Fl -guided
Ask each question on the terminal.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_LOG_DIR
Where the logs go; default
.Pa /var/log/installer .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/kldload/answers/TEMPLATE.env
Every answer, with its default, to copy; beside it, examples for a Fedora
desktop, a Debian server and a single-disk ZFS install.
.It Pa /var/log/installer/
On the live image:
.Pa kldload-installer.log
and one log per stage \(em
.Pa storage , zfs , security , network , bootstrap , bootloader
\(em with the answers as they were used in
.Pa effective-config.env .
.It Pa /etc/kldload/install-manifest.env
On the target: what was installed and asked for.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when installed; 1 on a failure, named; 129, 130 or 143 when stopped by a
hang-up, an interrupt or a termination signal.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Not run for this page, since it overwrites a disk:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# cp /etc/kldload/answers/TEMPLATE.env /root/my.env
# kldload-install-target --config /root/my.env
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kld 8 ,
.Xr kldload-autoinstall 8 ,
.Xr kldload-firstboot 8 ,
.Xr kldload-netboot-server 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-08-15 two machines installed
.Dq cleanly
and had no kernel: one optional package missing from the offline mirror
took the whole transaction with it.
On 2026-05-15 a false
.Dq Installation failed
line in the middle of a good install made operators abort it.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The disk named in the answers is overwritten without a further question.
